1
00:00:00,129 --> 00:00:02,299
Let me start with a situation
you might recognize.

2
00:00:02,449 --> 00:00:06,449
A customer calls BrightLeaf and asks,
"Do you have 200 rolls of stretch

3
00:00:06,489 --> 00:00:08,129
wrap I can collect tomorrow?"

4
00:00:08,169 --> 00:00:11,530
It sounds simple, but you need a
reliable stock number before you can

5
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:13,502
answer. Sales has a spreadsheet.

6
00:00:13,703 --> 00:00:15,842
The warehouse team checks
what's on the shelf.

7
00:00:15,882 --> 00:00:18,392
Procurement has purchase
orders sitting in email.

8
00:00:19,123 --> 00:00:22,572
Someone has to bring that information
together while the customer waits.

9
00:00:22,612 --> 00:00:25,412
If you have worked in supply
chain, you have probably dealt with

10
00:00:25,452 --> 00:00:29,280
something like that An ERP gives
those teams one shared system to work

11
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,754
from and that's where we
need to start with Stocky.

12
00:00:31,794 --> 00:00:35,163
If the stock number in the system is
wrong, Stocky could give Sarah the

13
00:00:35,203 --> 00:00:37,942
wrong advice even if the
answer sounds convincing.

14
00:00:38,071 --> 00:00:41,939
So in this video, I will walk you
through Odoo the ERP we will use

15
00:00:41,979 --> 00:00:42,812
throughout the course.

16
00:00:42,852 --> 00:00:46,582
We will set up your own trial, look
around the different apps and get

17
00:00:46,652 --> 00:00:49,870
comfortable with three terms,
module, record and field.

18
00:00:49,914 --> 00:00:53,532
Then we will add BrightLeaf's 10
products, their starting stock and

19
00:00:53,572 --> 00:00:54,667
their reorder points.

20
00:00:54,707 --> 00:00:57,215
That's the information
Stocky will work with later.

21
00:00:57,255 --> 00:01:00,692
You will have your own test system
to practice in so you can explore

22
00:01:00,732 --> 00:01:02,806
without affecting
anything at your company.

23
00:01:02,846 --> 00:01:06,275
And if you have never used an ERP
before don't worry, we will go through

24
00:01:06,315 --> 00:01:08,729
the setup together one step at a time.

25
00:01:08,769 --> 00:01:11,179
Let's go, get your Odoo account ready.

26
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:13,335
We're on odoo dot com.

27
00:01:13,375 --> 00:01:17,285
Odoo is an ERP used by millions of
businesses, and the good news for us

28
00:01:17,325 --> 00:01:19,763
is that it runs entirely in your browser.

29
00:01:20,375 --> 00:01:21,813
Nothing to install.

30
00:01:23,014 --> 00:01:25,364
First, let me explain the word.

31
00:01:25,977 --> 00:01:29,849
ERP stands for Enterprise Resource
Planning, which is a terrible name,

32
00:01:29,889 --> 00:01:34,424
so forget it. Here's what it really
is: the company's central filing

33
00:01:34,464 --> 00:01:36,114
cabinet plus its rulebook.

34
00:01:36,727 --> 00:01:40,674
Every department keeps its records
in one place, and the system enforces

35
00:01:40,714 --> 00:01:45,287
the rules. When the warehouse
receives fifty boxes, the stock number

36
00:01:45,327 --> 00:01:47,289
goes up for everyone, instantly.

37
00:01:47,902 --> 00:01:50,252
No emailing spreadsheets around.

38
00:01:51,448 --> 00:01:53,061
Let's create our own.

39
00:01:53,673 --> 00:01:55,898
Click "Start now It's free".

40
00:01:57,106 --> 00:01:59,231
Odoo asks which apps we want.

41
00:01:59,844 --> 00:02:03,281
Think of each app as a department's
drawer in the filing cabinet.

42
00:02:03,894 --> 00:02:08,219
For supply chain, we need three:
Inventory, for what's on the shelf.

43
00:02:08,831 --> 00:02:11,281
Purchase, for buying from suppliers.

44
00:02:11,894 --> 00:02:14,444
And Sales, for selling to customers.

45
00:02:15,056 --> 00:02:17,144
Tick those three and nothing else.

46
00:02:17,756 --> 00:02:21,116
Odoo will quietly add Contacts
as well, because both sales and

47
00:02:21,156 --> 00:02:23,794
purchasing need a list of
companies to deal with.

48
00:02:24,988 --> 00:02:26,151
Click Continue.

49
00:02:27,358 --> 00:02:28,883
Now the sign-up form.

50
00:02:29,496 --> 00:02:33,108
I'm filling it in as Sarah, but
you use your own name and email.

51
00:02:33,721 --> 00:02:37,518
For company name, type "BrightLeaf
Supplies", so your screen matches

52
00:02:37,558 --> 00:02:39,283
mine for the rest of the course.

53
00:02:39,896 --> 00:02:42,071
Pick your country and click Start now.

54
00:02:43,264 --> 00:02:45,689
Odoo is now building your database.

55
00:02:46,302 --> 00:02:47,877
This takes about a minute.

56
00:02:49,066 --> 00:02:53,704
And we're in. Before we do anything
else, look at the address bar.

57
00:02:54,316 --> 00:02:56,491
This web address is your Odoo's home.

58
00:02:57,104 --> 00:02:59,364
Mine is brightleaf-supplies
dot odoo dot com.

59
00:02:59,404 --> 00:03:01,079
Yours will be a bit different.

60
00:03:01,691 --> 00:03:06,066
And the first part, before dot odoo
dot com, is your database name.

61
00:03:07,252 --> 00:03:09,390
Write both of these down right now.

62
00:03:10,002 --> 00:03:12,800
There's a box for them on the Setup
Checklist sheet in your activity

63
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:17,712
workbook. In video six, when we
connect Stocky to Odoo, these are the

64
00:03:17,752 --> 00:03:19,752
first two things it asks for.

65
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:25,238
Odoo also sends you an email to confirm
your account and set a password.

66
00:03:25,850 --> 00:03:28,525
Do that now, so you can
log back in tomorrow.

67
00:03:29,728 --> 00:03:31,216
One more thing to know.

68
00:03:31,828 --> 00:03:34,328
The free trial lasts fifteen days.

69
00:03:34,941 --> 00:03:38,503
That's plenty for this course,
but if it runs out, don't panic.

70
00:03:39,116 --> 00:03:42,676
You can start a fresh trial with a
new email, and because we're going to

71
00:03:42,716 --> 00:03:46,176
load our products from an Excel
file, you'll be back to exactly this

72
00:03:46,216 --> 00:03:48,053
point in about five minutes.

73
00:03:49,258 --> 00:03:54,643
Last setup step. BrightLeaf buys
from suppliers in the US, Mexico,

74
00:03:54,683 --> 00:03:58,656
China and Dubai, and in this course
we'll keep all our prices in US

75
00:03:58,696 --> 00:04:03,468
dollars. Go to the Settings app,
type "currency" in the search box,

76
00:04:03,508 --> 00:04:06,071
and check that the main currency is USD.

77
00:04:06,683 --> 00:04:09,783
If it isn't, set it to USD and click Save.

78
00:04:10,972 --> 00:04:14,822
If your Odoo won't let you change it,
or you can't find it, don't worry.

79
00:04:15,435 --> 00:04:17,385
Just treat the numbers as dollars.

80
00:04:17,997 --> 00:04:20,347
Nothing in the course
depends on the symbol.

81
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:26,873
This is the home screen, and every
icon here is what ERP people call a

82
00:04:26,913 --> 00:04:32,025
module. A module is just one department's
drawer in the filing cabinet.

83
00:04:32,638 --> 00:04:36,363
Same cabinet, same data
underneath, different drawers.

84
00:04:37,558 --> 00:04:39,621
You'll notice a couple of extras.

85
00:04:40,233 --> 00:04:43,656
Invoicing appeared because sales
and purchases eventually turn into

86
00:04:43,696 --> 00:04:47,683
invoices. Discuss is Odoo's internal chat.

87
00:04:48,296 --> 00:04:50,421
We won't need them, so ignore them.

88
00:04:51,616 --> 00:04:55,141
Let's open the three drawers that
matter to a supply chain pro.

89
00:04:56,338 --> 00:05:01,151
First, Inventory. This is
Tom's world, the warehouse.

90
00:05:01,763 --> 00:05:05,785
These cards are the two directions
goods move: Receipts, things coming

91
00:05:05,826 --> 00:05:10,038
in from suppliers, and Delivery
Orders, things going out to customers.

92
00:05:11,236 --> 00:05:14,911
Along the top, you'll see the same
pattern in nearly every Odoo app.

93
00:05:15,524 --> 00:05:18,374
Operations, where the
day-to-day work happens.

94
00:05:18,986 --> 00:05:20,849
Products, your catalogue.

95
00:05:21,461 --> 00:05:23,849
Reporting, where you get numbers out.

96
00:05:24,461 --> 00:05:27,336
And Configuration, the rulebook settings.

97
00:05:27,949 --> 00:05:29,436
Remember that pattern.

98
00:05:30,049 --> 00:05:33,011
Once you know it in one app,
you know it in all of them.

99
00:05:34,198 --> 00:05:38,173
Next, Purchase. This is Sarah's drawer.

100
00:05:38,786 --> 00:05:43,198
The first thing you see is "Requests
for Quotation", or RFQ for short.

101
00:05:43,811 --> 00:05:48,486
In Odoo, every purchase starts
life as an RFQ, basically a draft.

102
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:52,846
When the supplier agrees and Sarah
confirms it, the same record becomes

103
00:05:52,886 --> 00:05:56,861
a Purchase Order. Same folder, new status.

104
00:05:57,473 --> 00:06:01,708
Keep that in mind, because in video
seven, Stocky will create these RFQs

105
00:06:01,748 --> 00:06:03,273
for Sarah to approve.

106
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:07,630
Sales works the same way,
but in the other direction.

107
00:06:08,243 --> 00:06:10,393
Quotations become Sales Orders.

108
00:06:11,578 --> 00:06:13,816
And Contacts is the shared address book.

109
00:06:14,428 --> 00:06:19,341
Customers, suppliers, even your own
company live here, all in one list.

110
00:06:19,953 --> 00:06:23,541
Notice there's no separate
"supplier list" and "customer list".

111
00:06:24,153 --> 00:06:26,191
A company is just a contact.

112
00:06:26,803 --> 00:06:30,303
Whether it's a supplier or a customer
depends on what you do with it.

113
00:06:31,492 --> 00:06:33,142
Here's why this matters.

114
00:06:33,755 --> 00:06:35,742
These drawers talk to each other.

115
00:06:36,355 --> 00:06:40,364
When Sarah confirms a purchase order,
Inventory automatically expects a

116
00:06:40,405 --> 00:06:45,452
receipt. When a salesperson confirms
an order, Inventory automatically

117
00:06:45,492 --> 00:06:46,692
prepares a delivery.

118
00:06:47,305 --> 00:06:49,930
One action, every department updated.

119
00:06:51,118 --> 00:06:55,128
That's also why an agent is so much
more powerful connected to an ERP

120
00:06:55,168 --> 00:06:57,031
than to a pile of spreadsheets.

121
00:06:57,643 --> 00:07:00,581
Stocky reads one place
and sees the whole truth.

122
00:07:10,170 --> 00:07:13,501
Now that you have seen the different
apps, let's go over those three

123
00:07:13,541 --> 00:07:15,924
terms, module, record, and fields.

124
00:07:15,964 --> 00:07:20,433
You will hear them in Odoo, SAP,
Oracle, and Microsoft Dynamics.

125
00:07:20,473 --> 00:07:23,279
The screen might look different,
but the ideas are the same.

126
00:07:23,319 --> 00:07:25,709
Think of the ERP as a filing cabinet.

127
00:07:26,028 --> 00:07:29,389
Each drawer is a module, like
inventory, purchase or sales.

128
00:07:29,429 --> 00:07:32,609
It groups together the information
and tasks for that part of the

129
00:07:32,649 --> 00:07:35,743
business. Inside each
drawer, you've got folders.

130
00:07:35,814 --> 00:07:37,316
Each folder is a record.

131
00:07:37,356 --> 00:07:41,267
So one product is a record, one
supplier is a record, a purchase order

132
00:07:41,307 --> 00:07:42,497
is another record.

133
00:07:43,284 --> 00:07:47,227
And inside each folder, there is
a form with labeled boxes, product

134
00:07:47,267 --> 00:07:50,390
name, cost, supplier, reorder point.

135
00:07:50,455 --> 00:07:52,768
Each of those pieces of
information is a field.

136
00:07:52,808 --> 00:07:56,568
If you are used to Excel, a record
is like a row and a field is like a

137
00:07:56,608 --> 00:07:59,637
column. A module is more like
a group of related sheets.

138
00:07:59,677 --> 00:08:01,757
This will help when we connect Stocky.

139
00:08:02,141 --> 00:08:06,150
Stocky will ask Odoo for specific
information, such as the quantity on

140
00:08:06,190 --> 00:08:07,612
hand for a particular product.

141
00:08:07,652 --> 00:08:10,855
It needs to know which record
to find and which field to read.

142
00:08:10,895 --> 00:08:14,460
Once you understand those terms, it's
easier to tell the agent what you

143
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:16,342
need and check what it's using.

144
00:08:16,382 --> 00:08:19,392
Let's create a product so
you can see this on the form.

145
00:08:20,367 --> 00:08:24,554
Let's create our first record by
hand, so you can see every field.

146
00:08:25,167 --> 00:08:29,342
Go to Inventory, then Products,
then Products again, and click New.

147
00:08:30,537 --> 00:08:32,837
This blank form is one empty folder.

148
00:08:33,449 --> 00:08:35,787
Let's fill it in with
BrightLeaf's best seller.

149
00:08:36,987 --> 00:08:41,012
Product name: Steel Hex Bolts
M10, box of one hundred.

150
00:08:41,624 --> 00:08:45,624
Just under the name, make sure both
"Sales" and "Purchase" are ticked.

151
00:08:46,237 --> 00:08:49,734
BrightLeaf buys these from a
supplier and sells them to customers,

152
00:08:49,774 --> 00:08:51,049
so both are true.

153
00:08:52,245 --> 00:08:55,455
Now the most important field on
this whole form, and the number one

154
00:08:55,495 --> 00:08:58,395
beginner mistake. Product Type.

155
00:08:59,007 --> 00:09:01,807
Choose "Goods", and then
tick "Track Inventory".

156
00:09:03,015 --> 00:09:06,062
If you forget that tick, Odoo will
happily let you buy and sell the

157
00:09:06,102 --> 00:09:08,215
product, but it will never count it.

158
00:09:08,827 --> 00:09:10,540
There will be no stock number.

159
00:09:11,152 --> 00:09:14,575
And when Stocky asks "how many bolts
do we have?", the answer will be

160
00:09:14,615 --> 00:09:15,840
nothing at all.

161
00:09:17,025 --> 00:09:20,447
If your Odoo shows a list with
"Storable Product" instead, choose

162
00:09:20,487 --> 00:09:21,687
"Storable Product".

163
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:23,825
It means the same thing.

164
00:09:25,011 --> 00:09:27,561
Sales Price: sixteen eighty-eight.

165
00:09:28,173 --> 00:09:29,948
Cost: twelve fifty.

166
00:09:30,561 --> 00:09:33,771
That's a thirty-five percent mark-up,
and your workbook shows you the

167
00:09:33,811 --> 00:09:34,886
calculation.

168
00:09:36,093 --> 00:09:40,628
Then the Reference field, your internal
reference: BL dash one zero zero

169
00:09:40,668 --> 00:09:44,730
one. This is your SKU, your product code.

170
00:09:45,343 --> 00:09:47,218
Please never skip this field.

171
00:09:47,830 --> 00:09:51,865
Product names change, people type
them differently, someone writes "M10

172
00:09:51,905 --> 00:09:54,793
bolts" and someone else
writes "Hex Bolt M10".

173
00:09:55,405 --> 00:09:59,618
But BL-1001 is always BL-1001.

174
00:10:00,230 --> 00:10:04,240
When Stocky talks about products, it
will use this code, so nothing gets

175
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:05,080
mixed up.

176
00:10:06,279 --> 00:10:07,841
Now the Purchase tab.

177
00:10:08,454 --> 00:10:10,929
This is where we tell
Odoo who we buy from.

178
00:10:11,541 --> 00:10:13,566
Click "Add a line" under Vendors.

179
00:10:14,179 --> 00:10:15,891
Type Apex Fasteners.

180
00:10:16,504 --> 00:10:19,691
It doesn't exist yet, so
Odoo offers to create it.

181
00:10:20,304 --> 00:10:21,404
Click Create.

182
00:10:22,593 --> 00:10:24,418
Price, twelve fifty.

183
00:10:25,030 --> 00:10:27,718
And delivery lead time, seven days.

184
00:10:28,330 --> 00:10:32,040
That's how long Apex usually takes
from order to arrival at our Columbus

185
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:35,755
warehouse. Lead time is gold for an agent.

186
00:10:36,368 --> 00:10:39,040
It's the difference between "you're
low" and "you're low and you have

187
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,993
seven days before it's a problem".

188
00:10:42,195 --> 00:10:44,720
Save, with this little cloud icon.

189
00:10:45,332 --> 00:10:47,645
And there it is: our first record.

190
00:10:48,257 --> 00:10:50,445
One folder in the Inventory drawer.

191
00:10:51,645 --> 00:10:53,820
Look at these buttons across the top.

192
00:10:54,432 --> 00:10:56,482
Odoo calls them smart buttons.

193
00:10:57,095 --> 00:11:00,582
On Hand says zero, because we
haven't received anything yet.

194
00:11:01,195 --> 00:11:03,170
We'll fix that in a few minutes.

195
00:11:04,359 --> 00:11:07,396
And here's that "drawers talk
to each other" idea again.

196
00:11:08,009 --> 00:11:11,506
We created Apex Fasteners from
inside a product, but it lives in

197
00:11:11,546 --> 00:11:13,759
Contacts, the shared address book.

198
00:11:14,371 --> 00:11:19,559
Let me add its city, Columbus, Ohio,
and the country, United States.

199
00:11:20,171 --> 00:11:24,484
In video eight, Stocky uses supplier
cities to check the local weather.

200
00:11:25,096 --> 00:11:27,384
So this little field will matter later.

201
00:11:29,933 --> 00:11:32,696
Typing one product took
us about three minutes.

202
00:11:33,308 --> 00:11:34,783
BrightLeaf has ten.

203
00:11:35,396 --> 00:11:37,996
Your company probably has ten thousand.

204
00:11:38,608 --> 00:11:40,821
Nobody types those in by hand.

205
00:11:41,433 --> 00:11:42,646
We import them.

206
00:11:43,847 --> 00:11:46,397
Here's the import file
from your resources.

207
00:11:47,010 --> 00:11:49,847
One row per product, one column per field.

208
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:54,682
Look at the column headers: Internal
Reference, Name, Product Type,

209
00:11:54,722 --> 00:11:57,647
Track Inventory, Sales Price, Cost.

210
00:11:58,260 --> 00:12:01,947
They are spelled exactly like the
field labels we just saw on the form.

211
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:06,982
That's on purpose. When the headers
match, Odoo matches the columns for

212
00:12:07,022 --> 00:12:07,572
you.

213
00:12:08,777 --> 00:12:13,815
Notice BL-1001 isn't in here,
because we just created it by hand.

214
00:12:14,427 --> 00:12:18,100
If we imported it again, we'd have
two bolt records, and that's the kind

215
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:21,127
of duplicate that confuses
humans and agents alike.

216
00:12:22,331 --> 00:12:24,794
Back in Odoo, on the Products list.

217
00:12:25,406 --> 00:12:29,129
Click the little menu icon, the
three dots next to the word Products,

218
00:12:29,169 --> 00:12:30,569
and choose "Import".

219
00:12:31,757 --> 00:12:34,482
Click Upload File and
choose the import workbook.

220
00:12:35,687 --> 00:12:38,262
And this is the screen I
want you to understand.

221
00:12:38,875 --> 00:12:41,300
On the left, your Excel columns.

222
00:12:41,912 --> 00:12:45,012
On the right, the Odoo
field each one will go into.

223
00:12:45,625 --> 00:12:49,022
Odoo has matched them all automatically,
because our headers match the

224
00:12:49,062 --> 00:12:50,225
field names.

225
00:12:51,425 --> 00:12:54,885
If one of your columns ever shows
"To import, select a field",

226
00:12:54,925 --> 00:12:58,198
or it's left blank, just click the
dropdown and pick the right field

227
00:12:58,238 --> 00:13:02,748
yourself. That's all mapping is:
telling Odoo which labelled box each

228
00:13:02,788 --> 00:13:04,188
column belongs in.

229
00:13:05,387 --> 00:13:08,150
Before importing, always click Test.

230
00:13:08,762 --> 00:13:11,387
Test checks every row
without saving anything.

231
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,322
If something's wrong, like a letter
in the price column, it tells you

232
00:13:15,362 --> 00:13:19,300
which row. Green banner,
everything seems valid.

233
00:13:20,501 --> 00:13:23,751
Now click Import. And there we go.

234
00:13:24,364 --> 00:13:30,299
Ten products. BL-1001 that we typed,
plus nine imported in about four

235
00:13:30,339 --> 00:13:31,251
seconds.

236
00:13:32,447 --> 00:13:33,860
Let's spot-check one.

237
00:13:34,472 --> 00:13:37,847
Pallet Jack Wheels, BL-1005.

238
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:42,532
Goods, inventory tracked, cost
thirty-eight, sales price fifty-one

239
00:13:42,572 --> 00:13:44,885
thirty. Perfect.

240
00:13:46,073 --> 00:13:50,608
Now try something. Use the search
bar at the top of the list and type

241
00:13:50,648 --> 00:13:56,148
"BL-100". Every product code
starting with BL-100 appears.

242
00:13:56,761 --> 00:14:00,198
That's the power of a
clean, consistent SKU code.

243
00:14:00,811 --> 00:14:03,198
Stocky will search exactly like this.

244
00:14:04,953 --> 00:14:08,573
Before we add the stock numbers, let
me explain why we have been careful

245
00:14:08,613 --> 00:14:09,697
with the product setup.

246
00:14:09,737 --> 00:14:13,637
A distributor I know set up an alert
for products that fell below their

247
00:14:13,677 --> 00:14:17,622
reorder point. It ran for 3 months
without flagging their biggest

248
00:14:17,662 --> 00:14:20,989
product. They discovered the problem
when they could not ship a major

249
00:14:21,029 --> 00:14:24,575
customer order. when they check the
setup inventory tracking had not

250
00:14:24,615 --> 00:14:28,638
been enabled for that product the
ERP was not counting it so the alert

251
00:14:28,678 --> 00:14:32,638
had no stock figure to check that's
an easy detail to miss you can still

252
00:14:32,678 --> 00:14:36,422
have the product in the system and
use it on orders without realizing

253
00:14:36,462 --> 00:14:39,876
that stock is not being tracked so
there are three things I want you to

254
00:14:39,916 --> 00:14:43,484
check First, make sure
inventory tracking is enabled.

255
00:14:43,842 --> 00:14:46,767
Second, use a consistent
SKU for each product.

256
00:14:46,807 --> 00:14:50,865
If the same item appears under
different names or codes, it's easy to

257
00:14:50,905 --> 00:14:52,635
end up with duplicate records.

258
00:14:52,690 --> 00:14:54,875
And third, enter the supplier's lead time.

259
00:14:54,915 --> 00:14:58,744
You need to know how long a replacement
order will take when the stock

260
00:14:58,784 --> 00:14:59,867
starts running low.

261
00:14:59,907 --> 00:15:03,832
All of this matters for Stocky too,
it could give Sarah an answer that

262
00:15:03,872 --> 00:15:07,451
sounds convincing while working
from the information that's wrong or

263
00:15:07,521 --> 00:15:10,889
incomplete. She might then make a
purchasing decision based on it.

264
00:15:11,339 --> 00:15:14,699
Getting these details right now will
help us avoid that when we start

265
00:15:14,739 --> 00:15:15,629
using the agent.

266
00:15:16,567 --> 00:15:19,442
Our products exist, but
the shelves are empty.

267
00:15:20,054 --> 00:15:22,429
Let's give BrightLeaf some starting stock.

268
00:15:23,042 --> 00:15:26,517
Go to Inventory, Operations,
Physical Inventory.

269
00:15:27,129 --> 00:15:29,929
This is the screen you'd
use after a stock count.

270
00:15:31,129 --> 00:15:36,041
Click New. Product: BL-1001, the bolts.

271
00:15:36,654 --> 00:15:40,991
Odoo puts it on WH slash Stock,
that's the main warehouse shelf.

272
00:15:41,604 --> 00:15:44,654
Counted quantity: one
hundred and forty-five.

273
00:15:45,266 --> 00:15:46,216
Then Apply.

274
00:15:47,419 --> 00:15:51,406
Pallet jack wheels, BL-1005: eighteen.

275
00:15:52,019 --> 00:15:53,781
And I'll speed through the rest.

276
00:15:54,394 --> 00:15:57,441
All ten numbers are on the "Starting
Stock and Reorder" sheet in your

277
00:15:57,481 --> 00:15:59,969
workbook, so you can copy them exactly.

278
00:16:01,165 --> 00:16:03,377
I've chosen these numbers on purpose.

279
00:16:03,990 --> 00:16:06,977
Four of our products are now
below their reorder point.

280
00:16:07,590 --> 00:16:12,240
Don't fix that. Those four are
Stocky's first job in video six.

281
00:16:13,447 --> 00:16:16,059
Now the rulebook part
of our filing cabinet.

282
00:16:16,672 --> 00:16:18,584
Open the pallet jack wheels.

283
00:16:19,197 --> 00:16:21,697
Click the smart button for reorder rules.

284
00:16:22,309 --> 00:16:25,894
Depending on your version it says
"Min Max" or shows a little refresh

285
00:16:25,934 --> 00:16:28,247
icon. Then New.

286
00:16:29,449 --> 00:16:31,736
Min quantity: twenty-five.

287
00:16:32,349 --> 00:16:34,999
That's BrightLeaf's reorder
point for the wheels.

288
00:16:35,611 --> 00:16:37,449
Max quantity: fifty.

289
00:16:38,061 --> 00:16:40,261
That's how high we want to refill to.

290
00:16:40,874 --> 00:16:44,361
At BrightLeaf, the Max is
simply double the reorder point.

291
00:16:45,547 --> 00:16:49,382
So the rule now reads: when wheels
drop below twenty-five sets,

292
00:16:49,422 --> 00:16:51,059
top them back up to fifty.

293
00:16:51,672 --> 00:16:56,084
We have eighteen. So Odoo
knows we need thirty-two more.

294
00:16:56,697 --> 00:17:00,472
And remember, these come from Shenzhen
with a twenty-one-day lead time.

295
00:17:01,084 --> 00:17:04,634
That's exactly the kind of product
that keeps Sarah awake at night.

296
00:17:05,821 --> 00:17:07,783
And here's where it pays off.

297
00:17:08,396 --> 00:17:11,358
Inventory, Operations, Replenishment.

298
00:17:11,971 --> 00:17:17,146
Odoo already shows BL-1005 with a
suggested "To Order" of thirty-two.

299
00:17:17,758 --> 00:17:21,756
Don't click Order. We're leaving
that decision for Stocky and Sarah

300
00:17:21,796 --> 00:17:23,108
later in the course.

301
00:17:24,295 --> 00:17:27,995
Add reorder rules for the other
nine products using your workbook.

302
00:17:28,607 --> 00:17:31,905
Once they are in, three more
products join the wheels below their

303
00:17:31,945 --> 00:17:35,930
reorder point: the shipping boxes,
the safety gloves and the hydraulic

304
00:17:35,970 --> 00:17:40,482
oil. It takes about five
minutes, and it's great practice.

305
00:17:41,689 --> 00:17:43,939
Last thing, and it's my favourite.

306
00:17:44,551 --> 00:17:49,026
Open the bolts, BL-1001,
and click "In slash Out".

307
00:17:49,639 --> 00:17:51,651
This is the product's paper trail.

308
00:17:52,264 --> 00:17:56,324
Every time stock moves in or out,
Odoo writes it down: the date,

309
00:17:56,364 --> 00:17:59,039
from where, to where,
how many and who did it.

310
00:18:00,235 --> 00:18:04,045
Right now there's just one line:
one hundred and forty-five boxes of

311
00:18:04,085 --> 00:18:07,760
bolts added by an inventory
adjustment, by Sarah, today.

312
00:18:08,372 --> 00:18:11,997
Once BrightLeaf starts buying
and selling, this list grows.

313
00:18:12,610 --> 00:18:17,110
Receipt from Apex. Delivery
to a customer in Toronto.

314
00:18:17,722 --> 00:18:19,610
Every move, forever.

315
00:18:20,797 --> 00:18:23,397
This is the rulebook side of the ERP.

316
00:18:24,009 --> 00:18:26,597
Nobody can quietly change a stock number.

317
00:18:27,209 --> 00:18:29,259
There's always a record of what happened.

318
00:18:29,872 --> 00:18:32,597
And for an agent, this history is gold.

319
00:18:33,209 --> 00:18:36,907
It's how Stocky will one day be
able to say, "we've used about forty

320
00:18:36,947 --> 00:18:40,532
boxes of bolts a week for the last
month, so a hundred and forty-five

321
00:18:40,572 --> 00:18:42,272
will last under four weeks.

322
00:18:42,884 --> 00:18:44,809
Fine for now, but watch it."

323
00:18:46,443 --> 00:18:49,145
All right, we have covered
quite a bit in this video.

324
00:18:49,185 --> 00:18:53,130
You have set up your own Odoo
system, added BrightLeaf's products,

325
00:18:53,237 --> 00:18:56,191
entered starting stock and
worked with Reorder rules.

326
00:18:56,231 --> 00:18:59,430
You have also seen how Odoo keeps
a record of a stock movement,

327
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:02,020
so you can go back and
see what's happened.

328
00:19:02,069 --> 00:19:05,645
Before we finish, there are three
things I'd like you to remember.

329
00:19:06,413 --> 00:19:10,723
First, an ERP gives the different
teams a shared place to work from.

330
00:19:10,889 --> 00:19:13,404
Think of the filing
cabinet and its rule book.

331
00:19:13,444 --> 00:19:16,819
The department have their own drawers,
but they are all using the same

332
00:19:16,859 --> 00:19:20,532
system. Second, remember
module, record and field.

333
00:19:20,621 --> 00:19:24,561
Those terms will come up again when
we tell Stocky where to look and

334
00:19:24,601 --> 00:19:28,978
what information to And third,
check your data, inventory tracking,

335
00:19:29,295 --> 00:19:33,183
consistent SKU codes and supplier
lead times all affect how useful the

336
00:19:33,223 --> 00:19:34,485
agent's answer will be.

337
00:19:34,525 --> 00:19:37,888
To finish this lesson, you
have got two activity files.

338
00:19:37,928 --> 00:19:41,848
Use the BrightLeaf Product Import
file to load the nine products as we

339
00:19:41,888 --> 00:19:43,118
did in the demonstration.

340
00:19:43,232 --> 00:19:47,512
The Odoo setup workbook has your
setup checklist, progress tracker and

341
00:19:47,552 --> 00:19:50,793
the starting stock and the reorder
values for all 10 products.

342
00:19:50,833 --> 00:19:53,786
It also has a sheet called "Map my ERP".

343
00:19:53,826 --> 00:19:55,312
Take some time with that one.

344
00:19:55,352 --> 00:19:58,762
Think about your own company
system and identify the modules,

345
00:19:59,092 --> 00:20:00,941
records and fields you use.

346
00:20:00,981 --> 00:20:04,441
That gives you a starting point for
deciding what your own agent could

347
00:20:04,481 --> 00:20:06,831
read. Then take the 10 question quiz.

348
00:20:06,988 --> 00:20:11,692
In video 3, we will look at how
Stocky talks to Odoo through an API.

349
00:20:11,732 --> 00:20:15,682
I will explain it using a restaurant
example so you can follow along

350
00:20:15,722 --> 00:20:16,983
without a technical background.

351
00:20:17,023 --> 00:20:18,433
I will see you in the next video.
